# docs/adr

Decisions that apply to all repositories and to the meta-repository itself. A decision for a single clone is recorded in that clone.

## Log

| Number | Decision | Status |
| --- | --- | --- |
| [0001](0001-clones-via-mise-bootstrap-repos.md) | Clones from the `repos.toml` registry through `[bootstrap.repos]` in mise, without submodules | accepted |
| [0002](0002-only-agents-md.md) | Only `AGENTS.md`, without `CLAUDE.md` | accepted |
| [0003](0003-planning-in-root-openspec.md) | All planning in the root OpenSpec | accepted |
| [0004](0004-agent-commit-push-opt-in.md) | The agent commits and pushes only with permission, never to `main` | accepted |

## Format

The file is named `<number>-<slug>.md`; the number has four digits and is never reused. The front matter has `status: accepted`; when revisited, the old decision gets `superseded` and a link to the new one instead of being deleted. The title states the decision itself. Then come a paragraph with the decision and its reason, a "Considered Options" section with the rejected options, and a "Consequences" section with the cost.

The record exists so the agent does not reopen a decision that was already made. An option that was considered and rejected is written down with its reason, so the agent will not propose it again.
